      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.13", "U5.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Net GND includes U5 pin 13 (LAN_PORT3_TX+) and pin 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX-).",
      "expected": "These Ethernet PHY differential pair pins should not be tied to ground; they should be connected to the RJ45 jack or left unconnected if unused.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U5 | SKYLAB SKW92A ... 5-port Ethernet switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting PHY outputs to ground can damage the SKW92A or at least prevent Ethernet port 3 from functioning.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R1"],
      "pins": ["R1.1", "R1.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(Q1-S)", "GND"],
      "observed": "R1 value is '0.47mohm' (0.47 milliohms).",
      "expected": "R1 should be 0.47 Ω per the specification and PDI reference.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R1\") (value \"0.47mohm\") ...)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R1 | 0.47 Ω current-sense resistor | EPD booster current-limit sense"}
      ],
      "impact": "The current-sense resistor is 1000x too low, so the boost converter's current-limit sense will be wrong, potentially causing overcurrent or malfunction.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "C11 pin 1 is on net 'unconnected-(C11-Pad1)' with no other connections; pin 2 is on GND. Its value is 0.1uF and its footprint is 'Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder' (an inductor footprint).",
      "expected": "A decoupling capacitor should connect between a supply rail and GND, and should use a capacitor footprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ...)"}
      ],
      "impact": "C11 is electrically open and provides no decoupling; the wrong footprint also prevents proper assembly.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: U5 Ethernet pins 13/14 are shorted to GND, R1 is 0.47mohm instead of 0.47Ω, and C11 is an open capacitor with an inductor footprint."
}

